1
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:11,693
Right now,

2
00:00:11,693 --> 00:00:13,920
you are spinning at hundreds of miles per hour,

3
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,567
and you don't feel a thing

4
00:00:15,717 --> 00:00:17,267
The Earth turns once every day,

5
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:19,187
and everything on it turns with it

6
00:00:19,337 --> 00:00:21,047
Every sunrise and every sunset,

7
00:00:21,047 --> 00:00:22,487
every day and every night,

8
00:00:22,487 --> 00:00:24,053
comes from this spin

9
00:00:24,203 --> 00:00:24,633
But what if,

10
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:25,833
one second from now,

11
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,452
the Earth just stopped?

12
00:00:27,602 --> 00:00:28,832
The answer is terrifying,

13
00:00:28,832 --> 00:00:30,283
and very strange

14
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:32,249
Let's find out what would happen

15
00:00:32,399 --> 00:00:33,268
In this episode,

16
00:00:33,268 --> 00:00:34,468
we'll stop the planet,

17
00:00:34,468 --> 00:00:35,628
and see what happens,

18
00:00:35,628 --> 00:00:37,388
second by second

19
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:43,350
The Earth spins once every twenty-four hours

20
00:00:43,816 --> 00:00:44,806
Strictly speaking,

21
00:00:44,806 --> 00:00:47,206
one full turn takes about twenty-three hours

22
00:00:47,206 --> 00:00:48,966
and fifty-six minutes

23
00:00:49,319 --> 00:00:50,069
At the equator,

24
00:00:50,069 --> 00:00:51,949
the ground is moving at about one thousand

25
00:00:51,949 --> 00:00:53,489
miles per hour

26
00:00:53,639 --> 00:00:55,269
That's faster than the speed of sound,

27
00:00:55,269 --> 00:00:57,869
and faster than most passenger jets

28
00:00:58,155 --> 00:00:59,305
In New York or Paris,

29
00:00:59,305 --> 00:01:01,385
it's still moving at more than six hundred

30
00:01:01,385 --> 00:01:02,975
miles per hour

31
00:01:03,125 --> 00:01:05,035
Only at the North and South Poles are you

32
00:01:05,035 --> 00:01:06,853
just turning on the spot

33
00:01:07,003 --> 00:01:07,913
And at the same time,

34
00:01:07,913 --> 00:01:10,273
the Earth races around the Sun at about

35
00:01:10,273 --> 00:01:12,673
sixty-seven thousand miles per hour

36
00:01:12,925 --> 00:01:13,755
We don't feel it,

37
00:01:13,755 --> 00:01:14,715
because the ground,

38
00:01:14,715 --> 00:01:17,315
the air and the oceans all move together

39
00:01:17,661 --> 00:01:19,331
It's like sitting in a smooth airplane

40
00:01:19,331 --> 00:01:21,291
You only feel the speed when it suddenly

41
00:01:21,291 --> 00:01:22,411
changes

42
00:01:22,643 --> 00:01:24,113
And that is exactly the problem,

43
00:01:24,113 --> 00:01:26,513
if the Earth ever stopped

44
00:01:29,883 --> 00:01:31,393
Now imagine the planet stops,

45
00:01:31,393 --> 00:01:32,513
instantly

46
00:01:32,736 --> 00:01:34,286
Not over days or hours,

47
00:01:34,286 --> 00:01:36,267
but in a single second

48
00:01:36,417 --> 00:01:37,087
The ground stops

49
00:01:37,087 --> 00:01:37,647
But you,

50
00:01:37,647 --> 00:01:39,944
the air and the oceans keep moving

51
00:01:40,094 --> 00:01:41,164
This is called inertia:

52
00:01:41,164 --> 00:01:42,644
moving things keep moving,

53
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:44,724
unless something stops them

54
00:01:44,994 --> 00:01:45,824
Near the equator,

55
00:01:45,824 --> 00:01:47,904
everything not attached to solid rock would be

56
00:01:47,904 --> 00:01:50,504
thrown east at a thousand miles per hour

57
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:52,820
That's about four times faster than the fastest

58
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:54,048
race car

59
00:01:54,198 --> 00:01:55,348
It would be like a car crash,

60
00:01:55,348 --> 00:01:56,971
for the whole planet

61
00:01:57,121 --> 00:01:57,471
People,

62
00:01:57,471 --> 00:02:00,071
cars and animals would be flung sideways

63
00:02:00,593 --> 00:02:01,023
Buildings,

64
00:02:01,023 --> 00:02:03,343
trees and even the top layer of soil would

65
00:02:03,343 --> 00:02:04,971
be torn away

66
00:02:05,121 --> 00:02:06,870
And the closer you were to the equator,

67
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:09,270
the worse it would be

68
00:02:12,217 --> 00:02:14,773
The atmosphere would keep rushing east too

69
00:02:14,923 --> 00:02:16,193
Air isn't fixed to the ground,

70
00:02:16,193 --> 00:02:18,187
so it would keep its speed

71
00:02:18,337 --> 00:02:20,207
That means winds far stronger than any

72
00:02:20,207 --> 00:02:21,967
hurricane in history

73
00:02:22,284 --> 00:02:24,554
The fastest wind gust ever measured was about

74
00:02:24,554 --> 00:02:26,474
two hundred and fifty miles per hour

75
00:02:26,474 --> 00:02:29,074
These winds would be about four times faster

76
00:02:29,599 --> 00:02:31,349
Winds like that would tear apart almost

77
00:02:31,349 --> 00:02:33,429
anything built by humans

78
00:02:33,884 --> 00:02:34,324
Rocks,

79
00:02:34,324 --> 00:02:36,524
sand and trees would be picked up and thrown

80
00:02:36,524 --> 00:02:38,146
across the land

81
00:02:38,296 --> 00:02:40,326
The rushing air would scour the land and stir

82
00:02:40,326 --> 00:02:42,406
up enormous dust storms

83
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,320
The sky could turn dark with dust for days

84
00:02:45,519 --> 00:02:47,389
Only places near the poles would escape the

85
00:02:47,389 --> 00:02:48,840
worst of it

86
00:02:48,990 --> 00:02:49,660
Because there,

87
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:51,660
the ground and the air were barely moving to

88
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:53,100
begin with

89
00:02:56,483 --> 00:02:58,806
The oceans would keep moving as well

90
00:02:58,956 --> 00:03:01,106
The oceans hold an enormous amount of water,

91
00:03:01,106 --> 00:03:03,706
all moving east at hundreds of miles per hour

92
00:03:04,356 --> 00:03:06,546
Giant waves would sweep over the coasts and

93
00:03:06,546 --> 00:03:08,119
race far inland

94
00:03:08,269 --> 00:03:08,939
On some coasts,

95
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:11,249
the water could pile up into waves taller than

96
00:03:11,249 --> 00:03:12,369
skyscrapers

97
00:03:12,519 --> 00:03:14,784
Cities near the sea would be swallowed

98
00:03:14,934 --> 00:03:16,444
On the other side of each ocean,

99
00:03:16,444 --> 00:03:18,918
the water would rush away from the shore

100
00:03:19,068 --> 00:03:20,698
Even the solid ground would feel it,

101
00:03:20,698 --> 00:03:23,298
with powerful earthquakes all around the world

102
00:03:23,863 --> 00:03:25,473
Earth's rock is not perfectly rigid

103
00:03:25,473 --> 00:03:28,073
The sudden stop would shake the whole planet

104
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:30,738
Volcanoes could be shaken awake

105
00:03:30,888 --> 00:03:33,488
And this is only the first day

106
00:03:36,683 --> 00:03:37,433
Without spinning,

107
00:03:37,433 --> 00:03:39,673
the Sun would no longer rise and set every

108
00:03:39,673 --> 00:03:40,620
day

109
00:03:40,770 --> 00:03:41,200
Instead,

110
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,720
the Sun would hang in the sky,

111
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,812
almost not moving at all

112
00:03:44,962 --> 00:03:46,672
As the Earth travels around the Sun,

113
00:03:46,672 --> 00:03:49,259
a single day would last a whole year

114
00:03:49,409 --> 00:03:50,799
It would creep across the sky,

115
00:03:50,799 --> 00:03:53,399
taking months to go from sunrise to sunset

116
00:03:54,193 --> 00:03:55,743
About six months of daylight,

117
00:03:55,743 --> 00:03:57,840
then six months of night

118
00:03:57,990 --> 00:03:59,060
One sunrise a year,

119
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:01,056
and one sunset a year

120
00:04:01,206 --> 00:04:03,806
The day side would bake under an endless Sun

121
00:04:04,028 --> 00:04:05,578
Temperatures there could climb higher than in

122
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:07,199
any desert today

123
00:04:07,349 --> 00:04:09,949
The night side would freeze in total darkness

124
00:04:10,402 --> 00:04:11,672
Without sunlight for months,

125
00:04:11,672 --> 00:04:14,272
it could become colder than Antarctica

126
00:04:17,717 --> 00:04:19,267
Here's something most people don't know:

127
00:04:19,267 --> 00:04:21,817
the Earth isn't a perfect ball

128
00:04:21,967 --> 00:04:22,797
Because it spins,

129
00:04:22,797 --> 00:04:24,197
it bulges around the middle,

130
00:04:24,197 --> 00:04:26,277
by about twenty-one kilometers

131
00:04:26,878 --> 00:04:28,748
The spin flings the oceans outward too,

132
00:04:28,748 --> 00:04:31,348
so there is extra water around the equator

133
00:04:31,743 --> 00:04:33,013
If you stand on the equator,

134
00:04:33,013 --> 00:04:34,773
you are actually farther from the Earth's

135
00:04:34,773 --> 00:04:36,691
center than at the poles

136
00:04:36,841 --> 00:04:37,631
Without the spin,

137
00:04:37,631 --> 00:04:39,831
the oceans would slowly flow away from the

138
00:04:39,831 --> 00:04:40,311
equator,

139
00:04:40,311 --> 00:04:41,800
toward the poles

140
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:43,860
The solid rock would slowly settle too,

141
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:46,328
but much more slowly than the water

142
00:04:46,478 --> 00:04:47,948
Two giant oceans would form,

143
00:04:47,948 --> 00:04:50,183
one at each end of the planet

144
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:52,523
The northern ocean would cover much of Canada,

145
00:04:52,523 --> 00:04:54,166
Europe and Russia

146
00:04:54,316 --> 00:04:55,146
And around the middle,

147
00:04:55,146 --> 00:04:57,146
a single super-continent would appear,

148
00:04:57,146 --> 00:04:59,746
stretching all the way around the world

149
00:05:00,028 --> 00:05:02,058
Underwater mountains and valleys would rise

150
00:05:02,058 --> 00:05:04,138
into the open air

151
00:05:07,283 --> 00:05:09,313
The Earth's spin is what makes big storms

152
00:05:09,313 --> 00:05:10,433
twist

153
00:05:10,639 --> 00:05:13,239
This is called the Coriolis effect

154
00:05:13,426 --> 00:05:15,456
It's also why storms in the north spin one

155
00:05:15,456 --> 00:05:15,656
way,

156
00:05:15,656 --> 00:05:18,256
and storms in the south spin the other way

157
00:05:18,442 --> 00:05:19,152
Without it,

158
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:21,712
hurricanes and typhoons as we know them would

159
00:05:21,712 --> 00:05:22,832
disappear

160
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:23,626
Instead,

161
00:05:23,626 --> 00:05:25,706
hot air from the day side would flow toward

162
00:05:25,706 --> 00:05:27,500
the freezing night side

163
00:05:27,650 --> 00:05:29,680
Cold air from the night side would rush back

164
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:31,157
along the ground

165
00:05:31,307 --> 00:05:33,907
Winds would blow in completely new directions

166
00:05:34,408 --> 00:05:36,758
Huge clouds and heavy rain could form above the

167
00:05:36,758 --> 00:05:37,558
hottest spot,

168
00:05:37,558 --> 00:05:40,158
where the Sun is directly overhead

169
00:05:40,399 --> 00:05:42,189
The weather would be unlike anything humans

170
00:05:42,189 --> 00:05:43,859
have ever seen

171
00:05:44,009 --> 00:05:46,679
Scientists study faraway planets that spin very

172
00:05:46,679 --> 00:05:47,199
slowly,

173
00:05:47,199 --> 00:05:49,799
to learn what this kind of weather is like

174
00:05:53,583 --> 00:05:54,493
Deep inside the Earth,

175
00:05:54,493 --> 00:05:56,907
molten metal flows in the outer core

176
00:05:57,057 --> 00:05:59,007
This liquid iron is nearly as hot as the

177
00:05:59,007 --> 00:06:00,669
surface of the Sun

178
00:06:00,819 --> 00:06:01,329
As it moves,

179
00:06:01,329 --> 00:06:03,169
it works like a giant generator,

180
00:06:03,169 --> 00:06:05,769
creating a magnetic field around the planet

181
00:06:06,056 --> 00:06:08,446
Scientists think the planet's spin helps keep

182
00:06:08,446 --> 00:06:10,526
our magnetic field strong

183
00:06:10,851 --> 00:06:11,601
Without the spin,

184
00:06:11,601 --> 00:06:13,872
that field could become much weaker

185
00:06:14,022 --> 00:06:15,252
Venus barely spins,

186
00:06:15,252 --> 00:06:17,532
taking two hundred and forty-three Earth days

187
00:06:17,532 --> 00:06:18,292
to turn once,

188
00:06:18,292 --> 00:06:20,892
and it has almost no magnetic field

189
00:06:21,174 --> 00:06:23,364
The magnetic field protects us from particles

190
00:06:23,364 --> 00:06:25,308
blasted out by the Sun

191
00:06:25,458 --> 00:06:26,648
Over a very long time,

192
00:06:26,648 --> 00:06:29,048
the solar wind could also strip away some of

193
00:06:29,048 --> 00:06:30,232
our air

194
00:06:30,382 --> 00:06:31,612
Compasses might stop working,

195
00:06:31,612 --> 00:06:33,132
and the northern lights could look very

196
00:06:33,132 --> 00:06:34,252
different

197
00:06:34,538 --> 00:06:36,768
Birds and sea turtles that use the magnetic

198
00:06:36,768 --> 00:06:39,368
field to find their way could get lost

199
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:44,100
If the stop was instant,

200
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:46,140
almost nothing on the surface would survive the

201
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:47,744
first few hours

202
00:06:47,894 --> 00:06:48,844
The safest place to be?

203
00:06:48,844 --> 00:06:50,524
Near the North or South Pole,

204
00:06:50,524 --> 00:06:52,818
where the ground was barely moving

205
00:06:52,968 --> 00:06:55,038
Scientists at a research station in the Arctic

206
00:06:55,038 --> 00:06:57,451
might feel only a gentle jolt

207
00:06:57,601 --> 00:06:58,711
People deep underground,

208
00:06:58,711 --> 00:06:59,911
in strong shelters,

209
00:06:59,911 --> 00:07:01,573
might also make it

210
00:07:01,723 --> 00:07:03,793
Deep mines or bunkers could protect them from

211
00:07:03,793 --> 00:07:05,790
the winds and flying debris

212
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:07,770
But then they'd face months of darkness,

213
00:07:07,770 --> 00:07:09,959
or months of burning sunlight

214
00:07:10,109 --> 00:07:11,579
Growing food would be very hard,

215
00:07:11,579 --> 00:07:14,179
with crops either frozen or scorched

216
00:07:14,382 --> 00:07:16,212
Survivors would have to live along the edge

217
00:07:16,212 --> 00:07:18,283
between day and night

218
00:07:18,433 --> 00:07:19,863
In that narrow twilight zone,

219
00:07:19,863 --> 00:07:22,045
the temperature might be just right

220
00:07:22,195 --> 00:07:23,705
But as the Earth moved around the Sun,

221
00:07:23,705 --> 00:07:25,025
that zone would move too,

222
00:07:25,025 --> 00:07:27,425
about seventy miles every day

223
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:33,380
Now imagine the Earth slowed down very gently,

224
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:35,421
over thousands of years

225
00:07:35,571 --> 00:07:36,961
There would be no giant winds,

226
00:07:36,961 --> 00:07:38,812
and no killer waves

227
00:07:38,962 --> 00:07:40,992
The oceans would still slowly flow toward the

228
00:07:40,992 --> 00:07:41,392
poles,

229
00:07:41,392 --> 00:07:43,770
as the bulge around the middle shrank

230
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:46,360
But the days would get longer and longer

231
00:07:46,510 --> 00:07:46,780
First,

232
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:48,060
days of thirty hours,

233
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:49,300
then a hundred hours,

234
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,740
then weeks

235
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:53,203
Our body clocks are tuned to a twenty-four-hour

236
00:07:53,203 --> 00:07:53,483
day,

237
00:07:53,483 --> 00:07:56,083
so humans would have to adapt too

238
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:58,510
Plants and animals would have to adapt to very

239
00:07:58,510 --> 00:08:00,990
long days and very long nights

240
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:02,970
Many plants open and close their leaves with

241
00:08:02,970 --> 00:08:03,370
the Sun,

242
00:08:03,370 --> 00:08:05,970
and could not survive weeks of darkness

243
00:08:06,191 --> 00:08:08,791
Many species would struggle to survive

244
00:08:09,151 --> 00:08:10,381
But humans might survive,

245
00:08:10,381 --> 00:08:11,381
with greenhouses,

246
00:08:11,381 --> 00:08:13,461
lights and underground farms

247
00:08:17,217 --> 00:08:17,967
Here's the twist:

248
00:08:17,967 --> 00:08:20,567
the Earth really is slowing down

249
00:08:20,747 --> 00:08:22,617
The Moon's gravity pulls on our oceans,

250
00:08:22,617 --> 00:08:24,673
and acts like a tiny brake

251
00:08:24,823 --> 00:08:27,093
The tides drag against the spinning planet,

252
00:08:27,093 --> 00:08:29,352
stealing a little of its speed

253
00:08:29,502 --> 00:08:31,532
That energy pushes the Moon farther away,

254
00:08:31,532 --> 00:08:33,932
about four centimeters every year

255
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:34,770
Each century,

256
00:08:34,770 --> 00:08:37,130
a day gets longer by about two thousandths of

257
00:08:37,130 --> 00:08:38,316
a second

258
00:08:38,466 --> 00:08:40,576
That's one reason scientists have sometimes

259
00:08:40,576 --> 00:08:43,042
added a leap second to our clocks

260
00:08:43,192 --> 00:08:43,742
Long ago,

261
00:08:43,742 --> 00:08:45,222
when the first animals appeared,

262
00:08:45,222 --> 00:08:47,822
a day lasted only about twenty-two hours

263
00:08:48,568 --> 00:08:49,318
Even earlier,

264
00:08:49,318 --> 00:08:50,798
when the Moon had just formed,

265
00:08:50,798 --> 00:08:53,398
a day may have lasted only a few hours

266
00:08:53,990 --> 00:08:55,460
Fossil corals show it too:

267
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:57,620
their growth rings record more days in each

268
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,020
year,

269
00:08:58,020 --> 00:09:00,273
hundreds of millions of years ago

270
00:09:00,423 --> 00:09:02,012
But it would take far longer than the Sun's

271
00:09:02,012 --> 00:09:04,612
lifetime for the Earth to stop

272
00:09:07,783 --> 00:09:08,013
So,

273
00:09:08,013 --> 00:09:10,455
could the Earth suddenly stop spinning?

274
00:09:10,605 --> 00:09:10,605
No

275
00:09:10,605 --> 00:09:12,515
There is nothing in our solar system that could

276
00:09:12,515 --> 00:09:14,194
stop it all at once

277
00:09:14,344 --> 00:09:16,694
Even a giant asteroid hit would barely change

278
00:09:16,694 --> 00:09:18,443
how fast it turns

279
00:09:18,593 --> 00:09:20,743
Our planet has been spinning for about four and

280
00:09:20,743 --> 00:09:22,647
a half billion years

281
00:09:22,797 --> 00:09:24,347
It got that spin when it formed,

282
00:09:24,347 --> 00:09:26,547
from a swirling cloud of gas and dust around

283
00:09:26,547 --> 00:09:27,918
the young Sun

284
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:28,578
In space,

285
00:09:28,578 --> 00:09:30,098
with nothing to slow it down,

286
00:09:30,098 --> 00:09:32,698
a spinning planet just keeps on spinning

287
00:09:32,945 --> 00:09:35,545
And it will keep on spinning for billions more

288
00:09:35,767 --> 00:09:37,317
Its spin gives us day and night,

289
00:09:37,317 --> 00:09:39,112
our winds and our weather

290
00:09:39,262 --> 00:09:41,372
It's one of the quiet reasons life on Earth

291
00:09:41,372 --> 00:09:42,758
is possible

292
00:09:42,908 --> 00:09:43,498
So tonight,

293
00:09:43,498 --> 00:09:44,378
when the Sun sets,

294
00:09:44,378 --> 00:09:44,858
remember:

295
00:09:44,858 --> 00:09:46,318
it's not the Sun that's moving

296
00:09:46,318 --> 00:09:47,758
It's you

297
00:09:48,550 --> 00:09:49,940
A thousand miles per hour

298
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:51,260
A day that lasts a year

299
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:53,660
Two oceans and one supercontinent

300
00:09:53,915 --> 00:09:55,765
And all of it depends on one simple thing:

301
00:09:55,765 --> 00:09:57,496
the spin under your feet

302
00:09:57,646 --> 00:09:59,483
Which what-if should I explore next?

303
00:09:59,633 --> 00:10:01,040
Tell me in the comments

304
00:10:01,190 --> 00:10:03,790
Subscribe so you don't miss the next episode
